{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden baseline of the MACHINE authorization surface as it stands before 114C.",
    "",
    "114C adds human principals and sessions on top of this. Its binding architecture",
    "says the four identity layers stay separate and that signed interactive mutations",
    "must require human authorization 'without weakening existing signature/policy/",
    "approval gates'. Nothing pinned those gates: VALID_ROLES appeared only in auth.rs,",
    "and ENDPOINT_AUTH_MATRIX.md is referenced from //! doc comments that assert routes",
    "'map 1:1' to it while no test reads the file.",
    "",
    "This fixture is the regression baseline 114C.0 owes. A change here is a change to",
    "who may do what on the cluster, and must be deliberate.",
    "",
    "Source of truth: crates/fabric-hub/src/auth.rs (VALID_ROLES, LEGACY_COMPAT_ROLES,",
    "required_roles). Regenerate only when the policy is intentionally changed.",
    "",
    "The /settings routes are NOT pinned here anymore: settings reads, and writes to",
    "the auth.* subtree, now also admit the human-only `admin` role (114D groundwork),",
    "which this machine-surface fixture's every_baseline_role_is_a_valid_role guard",
    "rejects by design. Their policy lives in human_account_route_policy_baseline.json."
  ],
  "captured": "2026-07-17",
  "source": "crates/fabric-hub/src/auth.rs",
  "work_item": "114",

  "valid_roles": ["dispatcher", "runner", "observer", "approver", "reviewer"],
  "legacy_compat_roles": ["dispatcher", "runner", "observer"],

  "_roles_comment": [
    "'runner' is machine-only. 114C forbids assigning it to a human account;",
    "that invariant is meaningless unless this vocabulary is fixed."
  ],

  "route_policy": [
